# Cases of tests/data/interp whose output differs from Bazel's recording (NAME.latin1.txt).
# Read by tests/java_recorded.rs `java_recorded_interp`: every other case must match Bazel line for
# line (printed output, SYNTAX lines, EVAL message, TRACE traceback); a listed case must still match
# in printed output and the kind of its first error (`text`), or may differ in kind (`kind`), and
# must be removed from this list once it matches. Reasons (third_party/starlark-rust/PATCHES.md,
# 0049-0055 and docs/starlark-errors.tsv):
#   more-syntax-errors  Java's parser recovers and reports every syntax error of the file;
#                       starlark-rust's stops at the first (its line is equal to Java's first).
#   location            same message, different file:line:column in the traceback.
#   text                different error text.
#   kind                different outcome (the probe runs no Blaze static checks and has no loader).
# Format: NAME text|kind REASON

